From d163573436d2394f4d050cb8e14d78eb4b5e37ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:21:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci(linux): build the Linux AppImage in a reproducible
 container

Add docker/Dockerfile and docker/Makefile defining the Linux build
environment (the build-linux apt packages plus SDL2/tinyxml2/libzip built from
source, frozen into image layers) and rewire the build-linux job to produce its
AppImage with `make -C docker appimage`.

The container mirrors the job's environment exactly; the only intended change
is freezing the floating `ubuntu-latest` runner and the from-source library
steps into image layers, so the build is reproducible and a developer can run
the identical build locally. The build still generates paperboat.o2r itself
(GeneratePortO2R), the build-name output and the packaged artifact are
unchanged, and release.yml (which calls this workflow) inherits the change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
